# FastAPI Backend

Sources: [fastapi.mdc](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules), [python-fastapi-cursorrules](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules)

## Structure (this repo)
```
backend/src/
  api/routes/       # thin HTTP handlers
  api/middleware/   # auth, rate limit, logging
  services/         # business logic
  data/             # repositories, stores
  containment/      # detection engine
  core/models/      # Pydantic event/session models
```

## API design
- Pydantic v2 models for request/response; declare `response_model=` on routes
- Use `HTTPException` with correct status codes; never leak stack traces to clients
- Async handlers for I/O; sync only for CPU-bound containment evaluation when appropriate
- OpenAPI tags match router modules (`Ingestion`, `Sessions`, `Metrics`)

## Dependencies
- Inject via FastAPI `Depends()`: DB session, Redis, `EventProcessor`, `SessionTracker`
- No global mutable state except documented singletons (telemetry bus, in-memory stores for dev)

## Validation & errors
- Validate at boundary; return 422 for schema errors, 401/403 for auth, 429 for rate limits
- Log security events at WARNING+; never log secrets, tokens, or raw tool-call PII

## Testing
- pytest + `TestClient` for route integration; unit-test detectors and scoring in isolation
- Fixtures in `backend/tests/conftest.py`; `ENVIRONMENT=testing` for in-memory repos
